values ('a9e2c6d4-1b58-4f07-8c31-5e0a3b7d9f16', 'organic-chemistry-biochemistry', 'Organic Chemistry / Biochemistry', 'This document curates a Year 2 undergraduate Organic Chemistry / Biochemistry course for Kinesiology. The course is a foundational requirement for movement-science programs, with core coverage of carbon structures, stereochemistry, organic reactions, biomolecules, enzyme kinetics, glycolysis, the TCA cycle, bioenergetics, and metabolism. The syllabus includes prerequisite chemistry review, pH and buffering, biochemical methods, nucleic acids and molecular adaptation, integrated metabolism, sport nutrition connections, and exercise-physiology applications. Designed as a 15-module second-year course for kinesiology students. Each module can map to one week in a semester format, with problem sets, molecular-model activities, short wet-lab or virtual-lab exercises, metabolism diagrams, nutrition claim critiques, and a final applied case.');

