ements, ergogenic aids, and safety"}, {"id": "d148c901-7dd4-43ad-905e-49a9f30ef12e", "type": "concept", "title": "Body composition, RED-S, diabetes, metabolic syndrome, and referral boundaries"}]}]}, {"id": "88c04dd7-a4a9-4ca2-8c8c-ac87553f3a6a", "type": "topic", "title": "Biochemical Methods, Data Interpretation, Case Applications, and Capstone", "description": "Apply course concepts through labs, data, clinical-exercise scenarios, nutrition claims, and integrative cases.", "children": [{"id": "3423b6c1-2b61-4b65-8c83-85268f881279", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Biochemical methods", "description": "Students learn how biochemical knowledge is measured rather than merely asserted.", "children": [{"id": "d976839e-e2d9-491a-96ad-2b7b761d2d18", "type": "concept", "title": "Spectrophotometry, chromatography, electrophoresis, and enzyme assays"}, {"id": "c4f40c67-50d3-4042-819e-cbc3b77ca109", "type": "concept", "title": "Blood glucose, lactate, ketones, lipids, hemoglobin, and creatine kinase"}, {"id": "cafcdf01-6d5a-495d-95e9-9fc5aa7a9b29", "type": "concept", "title": "Sample handling, controls, calibration, and error"}]}, {"id": "5b0f0075-587f-4ccc-a924-085f5e2d53d8", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Data and evidence literacy", "description": "This subtopic helps learners interpret graphs, claims, and lab results with care.", "children": [{"id": "bb9353ea-338d-477f-9a4f-eef1ec461fea", "type": "concept", "title": "Dose-response curves and Lineweaver-Burk limitations"}, {"id": "fa9e0dde-8ab3-4244-9918-179a5f980ad2", "type": "concept", "title": "Units, normalization, reference ranges, and biological variability"}, {"id": "df7a6647-424d-4271-bc1a-03bc434d7181", "type": "concept", "title": "Primary literature, supplement claims, and conflict of interest"}]}, {"id": "ec51688e-e08f-497d-8af2-3bf964e61e54", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Kinesiology capstone cases", "description": "Learners integrate organic chemistry and biochemistry with movement, nutrition, and physiology.", "